; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6694    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6695    \ACCEPT XF
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6696    \REASON The condition is for plausibility checks of the generated data. The code is verified by code inspection.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6697  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6698  \ID COV_COMM_MAGICNUMBER_CHECK
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6699    \ACCEPT XF
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6700    \REASON The condition is for magic number check of the post-build data. The code is verified by code inspection.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6701  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6702  \ID COV_COMM_FOR_LOOP_OPTIMIZATION
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6703    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6704    \ACCEPT TF tf tx
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6705    \REASON A run-time optimization to cut short a for loop using a break statement. The loop goes through an element list where exactly one element meets certain
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6706            conditions inside the loop. Once the element is found, the loop can be terminated to save run-time.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6707  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6708  \ID COV_COMM_SUBSET_OF_ELEMENTS
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6709    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6710    \ACCEPT XF
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6711    \REASON There is an iteration loop over elements such as channels or PNCs or signals and an action (e.g. an API call) has to be performed if an element has a
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6712            certain configuration parameter set to true. This parameter is used to select a subset of elements at run-time and it may be true for all relevant elements
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6713            in some configurations so that the run-time decision always returns true. An encapsulation of such run-time decisions would substantially degrade
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6714            readability of the code. The run-time decisions do not have an else branch.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6715  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6716  \ID COV_COMM_TIMER_INIT_VALUE_CAN_BE_ONE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6717    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6718    \ACCEPT TF tf tx tf
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6719    \REASON A timer value can be configured to exactly one main function period of the corresponding channel. In this case after decrementing the timer its value is always 0.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6720  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6721  \ID COV_COMM_COMMON_USER_WITH_MODE_NOTIFICATION
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6722    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6723    \REASON In some configurations a user can be mapped to all channels. If such a user has mode notification enabled,
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6724            every state change of a channel triggers a re-calculation of the lowest mode of this user.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6725  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6726  \ID COV_COMM_PNC_EXTENDED_NO_ERA_ON_ACTIVE_CHANNEL
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6727    \ACCEPT XF xf xx
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6728    \REASON In configurations with COMM_PNC_EXTENDED_FUNCTIONALITY_ENABLED == STD_ON it is possible to assign Gateway Type ACTIVE to so called additional channels (e.g. LIN)
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6729            in order to keep those channels awake via PNC. But ERA signals cannot be received on those channels.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6730  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6731  \ID COV_COMM_PNC_EXTENDED_SINGLE_ERA
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6732    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6733    \REASON In configurations with COMM_PNC_EXTENDED_FUNCTIONALITY_ENABLED == STD_ON it is possible to have only one ERA signal. When this ERA signal is received
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6734            and PNC bit is 0 the corresponding PNC system user shall be released. Note that having multiple ERA signals is the most common use case.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6735  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6736  \ID COV_COMM_PNC_EXTENDED_ALL_PNC_WITHOUT_CHANNELS
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6737    \ACCEPT TF tf tx
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6738    \REASON In configurations with COMM_PNC_EXTENDED_FUNCTIONALITY_ENABLED == STD_ON it is possible that all PNCs have no channels. Therefore all PNC users have no
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6739            connections to channels.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6740  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\ComM\ComM.c	  6741  \ID COV_COMM_PNC_ON_CHANNELS_NM_PASSIVE
